t_or_district","entity_name":"Ratcliffe-Allison-Pozer House","title":"Trace a House Built in Three Eras","subtitle":"Main Street corridor — Ratcliffe-Allison-Pozer House","notes":"Compare the house’s 1807, 1824, and 1927 sections, then follow the garden paths behind the residence.","short_summary":"Fairfax’s oldest residence reveals layered domestic and commercial history along Main Street.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fairfax identifies this as the city’s oldest residence, built in phases in 1807, 1824, and 1927, at 10386 Main Street.","source_url":"https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Fun-Facilities/Cultural-Arts-and-History/Ratcliffe-Allison-Pozer-House","source_title":"Ratcliffe-Allison-Pozer House","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":38.845976,"longitude":-77.304718,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"For 2026, the house is listed as open noon–2 p.m. on the second and last Saturdays from May through October and during select events.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-stacy-sherwood-community-center","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Stacy C. Sherwood Community Center","title":"Check the Community Arts Calendar","subtitle":"Blenheim Boulevard corridor — Stacy C. Sherwood Community Center","notes":"Look for a scheduled exhibit, film, or performance before going; public programming determines what visitors can enter.","short_summary":"A city community center provides dedicated rooms for exhibitions, rehearsals, and performances.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fairfax lists an art room, rehearsal space, and performance space at the Stacy C. Sherwood Community Center, 3740 Blenheim Boulevard.","source_url":"https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Fun-Facilities/Facilities/Rent-a-Venue/Stacy-C-Sherwood-Community-Center-Event-Venue","source_title":"Stacy C. Sherwood Community Center - Event Venue","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":38.8512185,"longitude":-77.299275,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Regular hours are listed as Monday–Friday 8:30 a.m.–8 p.m. and Saturday 9 a.m.–4 p.m.; specific programs may set separate access rules.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-historic-blenheim","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Historic Blenheim","title":"Study a Civil War Diary on the Walls","subtitle":"Blenheim Boulevard corridor — Historic Blenheim","notes":"Begin in the interpretive center to examine the accessible attic replica, then follow the signs around the historic grounds.","short_summary":"Preserved soldier inscriptions make this historic house a tangible primary-source site.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fairfax documents Civil War-era soldier graffiti inside Historic Blenheim and an accessible full-size attic replica in its interpretive center.","source_url":"https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Fun-Facilities/Cultural-Arts-and-History/Historic-Blenheim-Tours-and-History","source_title":"Historic Blenheim - Tours & History","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":38.8558675,"longitude":-77.2933379,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The page lists the center Wednesday–Saturday, 10 a.m.–3 p.m.; grounds are dawn to dusk. Check the posted renovation notice before visiting.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-van-dyck-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Van Dyck Park","title":"Choose a Court or Paved Loop","subtitle":"Blenheim Boulevard corridor — Van Dyck Park","notes":"Pick one activity before arriving: walk the paved trail, use a court, or meet at a pavilion within posted park hours.","short_summary":"A 36-acre recreation stop supports both an easy walk and several court sports.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fairfax describes Van Dyck Park as 36 acres and lists a paved trail, basketball, pickleball, tennis, volleyball, pavilions, and a playground.","source_url":"https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Fun-Facilities/Parks/Parks-Directory/Van-Dyck-Park","source_title":"Van Dyck Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":38.8525992,"longitude":-77.2983025,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The park is listed as open daily from dawn to dusk; pavilion reservations and organized uses may carry separate requirements.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gmu-daniels-run-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Daniels Run Park","title":"Follow the Wooded Trail Network","subtitle":"Embassy Lane corridor — Daniels Run Park","notes":"Enter from Embassy Lane with daylight to spare, and choose the paved route or an unpaved segment based on conditions.","short_summary":"A wooded 48-acre park provides a trail-focused break east of Old Town.","evidence_claim":"The City of Fairfax identifies Daniels Run Park as a 48-acre park with paved and unpaved trails, benches, picnic tables, and a playground.","source_url":"https://www.fairfaxva.gov/Fun-Facilities/Parks/Parks-Directory/Daniels-Run-Park","source_title":"Daniels Run Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":38.8472718,"longitude":-77.2916209,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The park is listed as open daily from dawn to dusk; consult current trail notices and avoid entering after dark.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
